   "author": "Hollowmere team",
   "story": "The Ashen kept a watch on this rise above Route 9 to see who came up from the Cordon gate: six watchers, a fire they never let die, and a pit full of what they took off the road. In March they caught a Remand salvager at the river and kept him in the cache pit to dig for them and read them the Program's papers. In May the fever came up from the campground with the trade goods. The Ashen did what the Ashen do: they barred their sick in the longhouse and stacked the pyre against its wall, strung the bone chimes across the burnt gap in the palisade and barred the gate. Nobody would light the pyre. The keeper went down into the pit to sit with the cache and the salvager until it was over, and the sick clawed their way out through the longhouse's east wall and lay down again where they had always slept. The old man they put up on the burial platform first still wears the cache key on a thong round its post.",
